<?php

declare(strict_types=1);

namespace App\Features\Deliberately;

use App\Platform\Auth\AuthenticatedTenantResolver;

/**
 * The auth layer has ONE entry point, and a feature module is not allowed to go round it.
 *
 * REPURPOSED AT TASK 5, and the rule it proves is now stronger than the one it replaced.
 * Until Task 5 this fixture imported the pre-Task-5 stub and the rule was "nothing may be
 * built on a class that is about to vanish" -- true, but temporary, and worthless the
 * moment the class went. QRPAGER-12 §6 required any rule that existed only to contain the
 * stub to be removed or deliberately repurposed rather than left pointing at a class that
 * no longer exists.
 *
 * What it proves now: a feature module may not reach into App\Platform\Auth at all. Not
 * the resolver, not the membership reader, not the device-token helper. A feature asks
 * "which tenant is this request" through the TenantResolver INTERFACE in Platform, reads
 * roles and abilities from the enums in Domain, and authorises through Gate -- so the
 * answer to that question has exactly one implementation and one place to audit it, which
 * is the property RequireTenantScope's docblock depends on.
 *
 * Importing the concrete resolver here is the violation deptrac must report.
 */
final class FeatureBuiltOnTheAuthStub
{
    public function __construct(private readonly AuthenticatedTenantResolver $resolver) {}
}
